  "snp5.19:0.2": "",
  "snp5.19:1.1": "According to SnA, the sixteen brahmans, after their questions were answered, requested and received the Going-forth and Acceptance. After that, Piṅgiya, now Ven. Piṅgiya, received permission from the Buddha to return to Bāvarī to report the results of their trip.",
  "snp5.19:1.2": "",
  "snp5.19:1.3": "",
  "snp5.19:1.4": "",
  "snp5.19:1.5": "Reading <i>nikkāmo nibbano nāgo</i> with the Sri Lankan and Burmese versions, a reading confirmed by Nd II. The Thai version has <i>nibbuto,</i> “unbound,” instead of <i>nibbano.</i> The PTS version has <i>nātho,</i> “protector,” instead of <i>nāgo.</i> According to Nd II, “no forest” here means free from the forests of passion, aversion, delusion, resentment, and all other unskillful mental fabrications. See <a href='https://suttacentral.net/dhp273-289#dhp283'>Dhp 283</a>.",
  "snp5.19:1.6": "",
  "snp5.19:2.1": "",
  "snp5.19:2.2": "",
  "snp5.19:2.3": "",
  "snp5.19:2.4": "",
  "snp5.19:3.1": "",
  "snp5.19:3.2": "See <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn35.82'>SN 35:82</a>, <a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn35.116'>SN 35:116</a>, and <a href='https://suttacentral.net/an4.45'>AN 4:45</a>.",
  "snp5.19:3.3": "",
  "snp5.19:3.4": "",
  "snp5.19:4.1": "",
